It is Saturday morning.
I normally volunteer at a café on Saturdays.
But Ludwig must not be alone.
I send a message to the café.
"I am taking the day off today," I write to them.
Now Ludwig and I have the whole morning together.
We go out into the courtyard behind my building.
I take out his little ball.
"Look at the ball, Ludwig!" I say to him.
I throw it across the grass.
"Fetch it!" I shout.
He runs fast and catches the ball.
"Come here!" I call.
He runs happily back to me.
"Give it to me," I say gently.
He lets go of the ball, and I pet him.
"You are a good dog," I say and smile.
I throw it again, and he fetches it.
I must take good care of him all weekend.
I am very happy that I stayed at home with him.
